; strokeundo.eval - a paint DRAG is one undo step, even when its first square
; already had the texture (editor-updates P0).
;
; The defect this pins: the undo step used to be decided on the PRESS. When the
; pressed square already wore the brush's texture nothing changed, the step was
; dropped, and every square the drag went on to paint had no undo at all - so
; Ctrl+Z skipped the drag and undid the edit BEFORE it instead.
;
; Read by geometry, not by message: `geomhash` fingerprints the level's surfaces,
; so "undo put it back" is a hash matching the one taken before.
;
;   H0 = the untouched level
;   H1 = after one square is painted (a plain place, its own step)
;   H2 = after a drag that STARTS on that square and paints three more
; then undo must give H1 (the drag alone came off), and undo again H0.

logecho on
reset
geomhash
echo --- place ---
editor place floors floor_slabs 5 5
geomhash
echo --- drag ---
editor drag floors floor_slabs 5 5 6 5 7 5 8 5
geomhash
echo --- undo the drag ---
undo
geomhash
echo --- undo the place ---
undo
geomhash
